ingcenter.com/about/","source_title":"About — Princeton Shopping Center","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Individual businesses set their own hours and purchase requirements.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"princeton-cemetery","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Princeton Cemetery","title":"Read Princeton’s historical markers","subtitle":"Greenview Avenue corridor · 29 Greenview Ave.","notes":"Approach along Greenview Avenue and use the cemetery’s historic setting for a quiet, respectful walk; treat it as an active burial ground.","short_summary":"A historic cemetery associated with national political and scientific figures.","evidence_claim":"Princeton Cemetery at 29 Greenview Avenue contains graves of a U.S. president, a vice president, and several Nobel laureates.","source_url":"https://250.mercercountynj.gov/visit/place/princeton-cemetery/","source_title":"Princeton Cemetery | Mercer County","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Be respectful of burial sites and posted cemetery rules.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"albert-einstein-house","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Albert Einstein House","title":"See Einstein’s former residence from the street","subtitle":"Mercer Street corridor · 112 Mercer St.","notes":"Walk Mercer Street for a streetside view of the house where Einstein lived from 1935 to 1955; it remains a private home.","short_summary":"Einstein’s longtime Princeton residence, viewable only from the public street.","evidence_claim":"Albert Einstein lived at 112 Mercer Street from 1935 to 1955; the residence is private and can be viewed from the street.","source_url":"https://princetonlibrary.org/guides/princeton-visitors-guide